<title>POLAND: POLISH LECH BREWER NO LONGER PUBLICLY TRADED.</title>
<headline>POLISH LECH BREWER NO LONGER PUBLICLY TRADED.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Securities Commission (KPW) withdrew Polish brewer Lech Browary Wielkopolski SA (Lech) shares from trade on Thursday, KPW said in a statement.</p>
<p>In June Lech asked the commission to remove it from the list of publicly traded firms seeking bourse entry as it no longer needed outside capital.</p>
<p>Lech said it expected to record sales of about 350 million zlotys this year against 250 million zlotys last year.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
